<section class="page-header">
<div class="container">
<p style="margin-bottom:8px;"><a href="/blog/" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.7);font-size:0.9rem;text-decoration:none;">&larr; Back to Blog</a></p>
<h1>New Year&#x27;s Eve Plans: Keep the Group Together in One Van</h1>
<p>One van, one sober driver, and everyone home safe. The easiest New Year&#x27;s resolution you&#x27;ll keep.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section">
<div class="container">
<div style="max-width:800px;margin:0 auto;">
<p>New Year's Eve falls on <strong>Thursday, December 31</strong>. Whether your group is headed to a supper club, a concert, a party across the county, or a friend's place out on a country road, the hardest part of the night is usually the drive home. Put everyone in one vehicle with one designated driver and that problem goes away.</p>
<h2>One van, one sober driver</h2>
<p>Pick your driver before the night starts. That person doesn't drink, holds the keys, and gets everybody home. It's simpler than coordinating five cars at 12:30 AM on icy roads, and it keeps everyone off the road who shouldn't be on it. Wisconsin takes impaired driving seriously, and so do we.</p>
<h2>Pick the size</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Up to 15 people:</strong> the <a href="/van-rental.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">15-passenger van</a> is $135/day plus $0.10/mile. A two-day rental covering New Year's Eve and New Year's Day with 80 miles of driving is about $278 before taxes and fees. Split ten ways, that's under $28 a person.</li>
<li><strong>Up to 7 people:</strong> the <a href="/blog/7-passenger-minivan-rental-black-river-falls.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">7-passenger minivan</a> is $78/day plus $0.10/mile.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Plan pickup and return around the holiday</h2>
<p>Hours can change around New Year's Eve and New Year's Day, so <strong>confirm pickup and return times when you book</strong>. After-hours drop-off returns are available, which makes a January 1 or January 2 return easy. Our regular hours are Monday to Friday 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM, Saturday 8:00 AM to noon, and Sunday closed. After-hours drop-off returns are available.</p>
<h2>What the driver needs</h2>
<p>The driver must be 21 or older with a valid U.S. driver's license, and there's no young-driver fee. The renter brings a Visa, Mastercard, or Discover credit or debit card linked to a checking account, and proof of full-coverage auto insurance. Riverside doesn't sell insurance.</p>
<p>We have one 15-passenger van, and New Year's weekend is a popular one. <strong>Call or text 715-396-1466</strong> to reserve. Happy New Year from the Riverside crew.</p>
<div style="margin-top:48px;">
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-list">
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">How much does a van cost for New Year&#x27;s Eve?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>The 15-passenger van is $135/day plus $0.10/mile. A two-day rental with 80 miles comes to about $278 before taxes and fees. The 7-passenger minivan is $78/day plus $0.10/mile.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Can I return the van on New Year&#x27;s Day?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>After-hours drop-off returns are available. Hours can change around New Year&#x27;s Eve and New Year&#x27;s Day, so confirm your return time when you book by calling 715-396-1466.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Who can drive the rental van?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>Drivers must be 21 or older with a valid U.S. driver&#x27;s license. Plan on one designated driver who doesn&#x27;t drink.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">How early should we book a van for New Year&#x27;s Eve?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>As early as possible. There is one 15-passenger van in the fleet, and New Year&#x27;s weekend is a busy one.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
